sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-chain-slc43a2a-lat4a-breaks-at-hypothesis> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The flying-fish candidate gene lat4a (ZFIN slc43a2a) has the weakest causal chain of the three fin-size genes: nothing experimental connects its amino-acid transport function to fin ray length, so that link is graded hypothesis, and every fin phenotype for the gene comes from a single publication" ;
    dct:description "Status: inconclusive. Chain strength is hypothesis, the weakest of the three fin-size genes; steps and grades: gene->molecular_function: mechanism; molecular_function->process: hypothesis; process->cell_or_tissue_effect: sufficiency; cell_or_tissue_effect->phenotype: sufficiency. The transport function is well supported but entirely from mammalian orthologs read as abstracts: LAT4 \"mediates system L activity when expressed in Xenopus laevis oocytes\" (Bodoy 2005) and functions as \"a symmetrical low affinity uniporter\" (Guetg 2015). Zebrafish Lat4a transport activity has never been measured. The step from that function to a growth process is empty of experiment: Daane 2021 only orders the gene, stating that \"the mechanism of fin-specific suppression of lof by lat4a mutations is occurring downstream of bioelectric signaling signals\". There is no mTOR readout, no amino-acid measurement in fin tissue, no substrate rescue and no transcriptional target. The phenotype end is real and quantified in that paper (shorter lepidotrichial segments; fin-type-specific suppression of the kcnh2a overgrowth), but all six ZFIN rows for this gene trace to the same publication, so the gene has no independent replication. What it does not establish: It does not refute a role for lat4a in fin size: the genetic interaction with kcnh2a is real and quantified. It establishes only that the mechanism between transport and ray length is unmeasured, and that the evidence rests on one laboratory and one paper. Pre-registration: none: a gap found while grading. The grading vocabulary was fixed in genotype/AGENT_BRIEF.md before the subagents ran." ;
    delphi:context "This is the gene the flying-fish paper implicates by convergent sequence evolution (F326L, present in both gliding halfbeaks and at least 7 of 9 flying-fish species), which makes the gap between its molecular function and its fin phenotype the most consequential gap in the project. The gain-of-function allele T200K was never assayed for transport, so even the direction of its effect on amino-acid movement is unknown." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-slc43a2a-lat4a-breaks-at-hypothesis> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-genotype-thread-claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-slc43a2a-lat4a-breaks-at-hypothesis> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Graded causal chain for slc43a2a (lat4a) and the publications behind each link" ;
    dct:description "Read from genotype/causal-chains.json, gene slc43a2a." ;
    delphi:statisticalTest "Literature chain construction and grading under genotype/AGENT_BRIEF.md; merged and validated by genotype/assemble_chains.py. No new experiment." ;
    dct:source <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15659399/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25480797/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32841365/>, <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34534441/> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom sub:chains ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/genotype/data.json> .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15659399/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Identification of LAT4, a novel amino acid transporter with system L activity." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Bodoy S 2005 J Biol Chem" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 15659399" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "In the present study we present a new cDNA, designated LAT4, which also mediates system L activity when expressed in Xenopus laevis oocytes." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25480797/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Essential amino acid transporter Lat4 (Slc43a2) is required for mouse development." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Guetg A 2015 J Physiol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 25480797" , "doi:10.1113/jphysiol.2014.283960" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "Experiments using Xenopus laevis oocytes demonstrated that Lat4 functioned as a symmetrical low affinity uniporter with a K0.5 of ~5 mm for both in- and efflux." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32841365/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Tissue-specific deletion of mouse basolateral uniporter LAT4 (Slc43a2) reveals its crucial role in small intestine and kidney amino acid transport." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Rajendran A 2020 J Physiol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 32841365" , "doi:10.1113/JP280234" ;
    delphi:context "abstract only: the full text could not be fetched" ;
    rdfs:comment "LAT4 is a broadly expressed uniporter selective for essential branched chain amino acids, methionine and phenylalanine, which are involved in epithelial transport." .
  <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34534441/> a prov:Entity ;
    dct:title "Modulation of bioelectric cues in the evolution of flying fishes." ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Daane JM 2021 Curr Biol" ;
    dct:identifier "PMID 34534441" , "doi:10.1016/j.cub.2021.08.054" ;
    delphi:context "full text read" ;
    rdfs:comment "Mammalian Lat4 shuttles isoleucine, leucine, methionine, and phenylalanine into the cell in an ion- and pH-independent manner.16 Lat4 has been linked to overall body size in mice,17 but its role in proportion or patterning is not known." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-slc43a2a-lat4a-breaks-at-hypothesis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m0 .
  sub:m0 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "status" ; schema:value "inconclusive" ; schema:description "status of this record in the words of AGENTS.md (supported, refuted, mixed, inconclusive, or a descriptive status)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/genotype-chain-slc43a2a-lat4a-breaks-at-hypothesis> schema:additionalProperty sub:m1 .
  sub:m1 a schema:PropertyValue ; schema:propertyID "chain_steps" ; schema:value "4"^^xsd:integer ; schema:description "links on the chain" .
